Source: pugl
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), meson, ninja-build, pkgconf, libx11-dev, libxext-dev, libxrandr-dev,
 libxcursor-dev, libgl-dev, libcairo2-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://gitlab.com/lv2/pugl
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libpugl0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: minimal portable API for embeddable GUIs
 Pugl opens a window, embedded in a host's or on its own, and delivers its
 events; drawing is left to a backend: OpenGL, Cairo or none. These are its
 X11 libraries, one per backend.

Package: libpugl-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libpugl0 (= ${binary:Version}), libx11-dev, libxext-dev, libxrandr-dev, libxcursor-dev, libgl-dev,
 libcairo2-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: minimal portable API for embeddable GUIs, development files
 The headers and the pkg-config files of pugl (pugl-0, pugl-gl-0,
 pugl-cairo-0), for building against it.
